00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:18,220
for all your help Emporio sure
but I can't go further please

253
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:24,857
I want your father to come back
to life, back to consciousness,

254
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:26,117
because if he does so,

255
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:29,847
then I think we can start to see
some hope in our world again.

256
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:37,117
Shit! Aw, damn it!

257
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,937
What the hell is up with this can of cola?

258
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,255
You just touched my drink, didn't you?

259
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:45,657
Didn't you shake or touch this
can when I wasn't looking?

260
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,777
Well, you better go get
me a new one now, inmate!

261
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:48,690
As if.

262
00:15:48,773 --> 00:15:50,014
No way I'd touch that.

263
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:53,356
The only thing I touched was
your little saucer plate.

264
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:57,357
My right shoe has a big
old hole in its heel.

265
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,270
Can't you see it?

266
00:15:58,353 --> 00:15:59,757
It's a bit of a safety hazard.

267
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,958
So I'd really like to get
it repaired at the factory.

268
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:06,677
Did you not hear me?

269
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,197
I spilled my cola because of you!

270
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:09,868
So where's that damn towel?

271
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:21,710
Wait,

272
00:16:21,793 --> 00:16:25,946
are you seriously telling me I need to
go buy you another can of soda right now?

273
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:29,457
And then I need to pour
it in your cup for you?

274
00:16:29,540 --> 00:16:31,077
Come on, man, that's ridiculous.

275
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,042
Why don't you do this on your...

276
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,450
What?

277
00:16:49,533 --> 00:16:50,363
What is this?

278
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,196
Here's what I'm looking for, a towel.

279
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:57,006
You can go now, but you have to
be back here within 20 minutes.

280
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,380
Huh? What the?

281
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,718
She's already gone?

282
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:03,000
Hang on a sec, where's my cup and saucer?

283
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,140
What the hell is all of this?

284
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,580
Could it really be?

285
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,760
What the?

286
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,374
The card saucer is floating in the air!

287
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,049
The cup and my boots, too!

288
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:20,618
For some reason, the cola
isn't splashing everywhere.

289
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,505
It's floating balls of liquid!

290
00:17:22,980 --> 00:17:27,437
Every single thing I touch inexplicably
becomes unmoored, suspended in the air!

291
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:31,579
Like this $50 bill floated itself
straight out of the guard's pocket.

292
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:32,900
And even myself.

293
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,140
But since when?

294
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:38,457
Did all of this weird stuff begin when
that strange guy started to chase after me?

295
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:41,177
During his pursuit, he spit
some sort of substance at me.

296
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:42,090
Is that why?

297
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,040
The disc!

298
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:48,380
Oh no, it fell out
because my body flipped!

299
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,400
Stone Ocean!

300
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:52,820
Just my luck.

301
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,537
Why can't I control my thread?

302
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:56,297
I don't have any sense of direction.

303
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:57,210
Up or down.

304
00:17:57,293 --> 00:17:58,512
There's no gravity here.

305
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:02,340
I must be in a zero-gravity
zone going to the men's prison

306
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:05,940
All right, then proceed ahead

307
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:16,700
That guy he's gonna take the desk
because I put my full strength into it.

308
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:17,900
I lost my balance

309
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:19,800
Gotta focus on this.

310
00:18:20,340 --> 00:18:22,440
Go in one direction like a rocket!

311
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:33,980
Hey, what the hell?

312
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:42,280
Well, damn it, stupid disc.

313
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,040
I can't destroy it.

314
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:47,420
It bounces back into shape,
like some type of rubber.

315
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:50,317
That's probably the reason why Palesnake

316
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,165
instructed me to just
collect the disc for him.

317
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:56,520
No way!

318
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:02,180
Hey, weather forecast!

319
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:04,197
Don't go any further away from me!

320
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,110
Can you hear me?

321
00:19:05,193 --> 00:19:06,551
I'm being attacked again!

322
00:19:16,620 --> 00:19:17,450
No!

323
00:19:17,533 --> 00:19:18,960
My voice doesn't reach him!

324
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,146
Nah, somebody got in the way.

325
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:33,237
And here I was, thinking that I was
only going to have to kill that woman,

326
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:34,200
Jolene Cujo.

327
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:40,120
Prepare for Jumpin' Jack Spark!

328
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:43,311
Weather forecast, listen!

329
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:45,459
His stand power is gravity removal!

330
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:47,717
And don't touch whatever
it is he shoots at you!

331
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:50,741
Try to dodge it, or else
you'll become weightless!

332
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,377
Zero gravity zone.

333
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:57,720
If you truly are a stand user, then you
should be fully aware what it is this means.

334
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,472
So, do you think you can figure that out?

335
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:10,720
What you've just thrown at me
looks like a piece of garbage.

336
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,360
This weather forecast guy,

337
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,365
he's apparently very powerful,

338
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:20,225
but his ability to control the
weather is still a mystery to me.

339
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:24,137
That cloud cover he summoned is probably
working as an atmospheric layer.

340
00:20:24,220 --> 00:20:27,977
He simply reflected away our
enemies attack with that resistance.

341
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:31,200
And that man's arm spin
has centrifugal force.

342
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:35,417
Since it's weightless, he can accelerate
forever with that spinning force.

343
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:38,677
Which would mean, since the
core of his body stays still,

344
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:41,113
he can accurately aim with strong power.

345
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:46,560
Jumpin' Jack Spark!

346
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:48,280
No weather forecast!

347
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:52,170
Fire?

348
00:20:52,253 --> 00:20:53,857
Where did this fire come from?

349
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:55,352
Air resistance friction?

350
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:57,097
This is seriously not good.

351
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:58,717
It's spreading all over my body now.

352
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,271
Release the zero gravity!

353
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:04,700
This is the end for you.

354
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:08,740
The abnormality alarm has
been activated in Hallway 7B.

355
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,860
I repeat, the abnormality
alarm... Oh shit.

356
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,557
Must have been the impact.

357
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,957
I've retrieved the damn disk and yet...

358
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:17,216
The gate is closing.

359
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,157
What should I do?

360
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:21,237
It's getting even harder
to go to the courtyard now.

361
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,957
But we have no other choice!

362
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:25,117
The enemy will be trapped in here, too!

363
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:27,024
It's my chance to get the disc!

364
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,340
What? No!

365
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:37,160
What in the hell?!

366
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:40,880
Everything that you touch,

367
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:44,520
if I'm right, it becomes weightless.

368
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:46,580
Am I correct?

369
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:49,060
Jolene Cujo.

370
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,620
The courtyard is just up ahead.

371
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:13,554
Still though, where is that
anti-gravity-wielding thief?

372
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:15,367
I need to get the disc back!

373
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:30,320
Although you think I cope

374
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:35,260
My head is filled with hope

375
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:43,740
Of some place other than here

376
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:50,240
Although you think I smile

377
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:55,360
Inside and all the while

378
00:22:57,080 --> 00:23:03,440
I'm wondering about my destiny?

379
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,897
I'm thinking

380
00:23:07,980 --> 00:23:13,597
about all the

381
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:18,457
things I'd like

382
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:24,480
to do in my life.

383
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:29,420
I'm a dreamer.

384
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:34,260
A distant dreamer.

385
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:39,460
Dreaming far away.

386
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,560
From today!

387
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,310
Thank you.

388
00:24:24,900 --> 00:24:26,260
Thank you.
